---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { product, publicRoutes } from '@content/site';

const page = publicRoutes.find((route) => route.path === '/data-deletion')!;
---

<BaseLayout title={page.title} description={page.description}>
  <section class="page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Last updated May 31, 2026</p>
    <h1>Data Retention and Deletion Policy</h1>
    <p>
      This policy explains how Clarity retains, deletes, and handles requests related to personal
      data, financial account data, and product records. It is intended for users, partners, and
      compliance reviewers evaluating Clarity's data practices.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy should be read together with the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which
      explains what Clarity collects, how data is used, and how service providers may process data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="purpose-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">1. Introduction / Purpose</p>
      <h2 id="purpose-heading">Clarity keeps data only as long as it is needed for the product.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Clarity is an early-stage personal AI financial co-pilot operated by a solo founder. The
        product is designed to help users understand their own financial context, including
        accounts, transactions, budgets, categories, goals, and conversations with Rex, the
        assistant inside Clarity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clarity's retention approach is to keep user data for as long as needed to provide the
        service, comply with user instructions, maintain security and reliability, meet legal
        obligations, and support legitimate operational needs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="collect-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">2. Data We Collect and Retain</p>
      <h2 id="collect-heading">Data is tied to the account and features a user chooses to use.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Account and profile data</h3>
        <p>
          Name, email address, authentication records, app preferences, account metadata, support
          requests, waitlist records, and privacy or deletion request correspondence.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Financial product data</h3>
        <p>
          User-authorized or user-imported account information, balances, transactions, categories,
          budgets, statements, financial role labels, and related financial context.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Assistant and operational data</h3>
        <p>
          Rex conversations, approved memory, goals, plans, voice transcripts if used, generated
          responses, security logs, diagnostic metadata, and system records needed to operate the
          service.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="retention-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">3. Retention Periods</p>
      <h2 id="retention-heading">Retention depends on the type of record and why it is needed.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Active account and product data:</strong> retained while the user's account is
          active or until the user deletes the data or requests deletion.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Connected or imported financial data:</strong> retained while needed to provide
          account, transaction, budget, categorization, and assistant features, unless removed by
          the user or deleted through a verified request.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Support, privacy, and deletion records:</strong> retained as needed to document
          and respond to requests, generally up to three years unless a longer period is required.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Security, audit, and diagnostic logs:</strong> retained for security, abuse
          prevention, debugging, reliability, and legal purposes, generally up to twelve months.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Backups:</strong> may retain deleted data for a limited period, generally up to
          ninety days, before backup rotation removes it from backup systems.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="request-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">4. How to Request Deletion</p>
      <h2 id="request-heading">Users may request deletion through the published contact path.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        To request deletion of your Clarity account or product data, use the
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page and choose <strong>Data deletion</strong>, or email
        <a href={`mailto:${product.supportEmail}`}>{product.supportEmail}</a> with the subject
        <strong>Data deletion request</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please contact Clarity from the email address associated with your account when possible.
        Do not send bank passwords, full account numbers, card numbers, Social Security numbers,
        one-time codes, API keys, screenshots, CSV files, or sensitive financial documents through
        public forms or email.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="after-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">5. What Happens After a Deletion Request</p>
      <h2 id="after-heading">Clarity verifies the request and deletes eligible records.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        After receiving a deletion request, Clarity may take reasonable steps to verify the
        requester's identity and confirm the scope of the request. Once verified, Clarity will
        delete or de-identify eligible account, financial, assistant, and product records from
        active systems as reasonably practicable, generally within thirty days unless the request is
        complex or an exception applies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Disconnecting a financial account is different from deleting stored data. Disconnecting may
        stop future access through an account connection provider, while historical data already in
        Clarity may remain until removed through product controls or a deletion request.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="exceptions-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">6. Exceptions</p>
      <h2 id="exceptions-heading">Some information may be retained when necessary.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Clarity may retain limited information where needed to comply with law, resolve disputes,
        enforce terms, prevent fraud or abuse, maintain security, investigate incidents, preserve
        audit records, process support requests, or complete backup rotation. Service providers may
        also retain information according to their own legal obligations, terms, retention
        schedules, and security practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        When Clarity retains information under an exception, it will aim to retain only what is
        reasonably necessary for the applicable purpose.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">7. Contact Information</p>
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Questions and deletion requests may be sent to Clarity.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        For deletion requests, privacy questions, or data retention questions, contact Clarity at
        <a href={`mailto:${product.supportEmail}`}>{product.supportEmail}</a> or use the
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
      <p>
        For more detail about collection, use, sharing, and user choices, review the
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
